[chrome]   Usage: chrome_crashpad_handler [OPTION]...
[chrome]   Crashpad's exception handler server.
[chrome]   
[chrome]         --annotation=KEY=VALUE  set a process annotation in each crash report
[chrome]         --attachment=FILE_PATH  attach specified file to each crash report
[chrome]                                 at the time of the crash
[chrome]         --database=PATH         store the crash report database at PATH
[chrome]         --initial-client-fd=FD  a socket connected to a client.
[chrome]         --metrics-dir=DIR       store metrics files in DIR (only in Chromium)
[chrome]         --monitor-self          run a second handler to catch crashes in the first
[chrome]         --monitor-self-annotation=KEY=VALUE
[chrome]                                 set a module annotation in the handler
[chrome]         --monitor-self-argument=ARGUMENT
[chrome]                                 provide additional arguments to the second handler
[chrome]         --no-identify-client-via-url
[chrome]                                 when uploading crash report, don't add
[chrome]                                 client-identifying arguments to URL
[chrome]         --no-periodic-tasks     don't scan for new reports or prune the database
[chrome]         --no-rate-limit         don't rate limit crash uploads
[chrome]         --no-upload-gzip        don't use gzip compression when uploading
[chrome]         --sanitization-information=SANITIZATION_INFORMATION_ADDRESS
[chrome]                                 the address of a SanitizationInformation struct.
[chrome]         --shared-client-connection the file descriptor provided by
[chrome]                                 --initial-client-fd is shared among multiple
[chrome]                                 clients
[chrome]         --trace-parent-with-exception=EXCEPTION_INFORMATION_ADDRESS
[chrome]                                 request a dump for the handler's parent process
[chrome]         --url=URL               send crash reports to this Breakpad server URL,
[chrome]                                 only if uploads are enabled for the database
[chrome]         --help                  display this help and exit
[chrome]         --version               output version information and exit
[chrome]   
[chrome]   Report chrome_crashpad_handler bugs to
[chrome]   https://crashpad.chromium.org/bug/new
